From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tseng <tseng.jayj@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:40:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: preserve current MeepCoin source baseline

Preserve the exact pre-correction MeepCoin daemon source as a committed baseline,
with no semantic change of any kind. Every byte here is what was already in the
working tree; nothing was reformatted, rewritten, or "cleaned up" on the way in.

The checkout is Monero v0.18.5.1 (commit 4f92268d7c16741cfb41e5bbe2aa46cc260a9ea5,
tree efd33e23973d17c05b16d844151d4b560dc1173c, from
https://github.com/monero-project/monero.git) with MeepCoin carried as uncommitted
work on top. That state was reproducible only from this one machine's working
directory, which is not a basis for reviewing consensus code. This commit makes it
a reviewable object; the companion lock in the main repository makes it
reconstructible from the pinned official base.

Staged as an explicit path list: the 20 modified tracked files and the 17 new
MeepCoin source files (src/crypto/meep-hash.{cpp,h} and the 15 regular files
directly under src/meepcoin_genesis/).

external/miniupnp is deliberately NOT part of this commit. It is a separate nested
checkout (544e6fcc73c5ad9af48a8985c94f0f1d742ef2e0 from
https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp), it is not a submodule of this base, it is
not referenced by any MeepCoin source file, and vendoring it here would silently
enlarge the reviewed surface.

No consensus behaviour is changed by this commit. The inherited Monero trust
anchors it captures -- the height-202612 long-hash exception, the historical
block-ID remap, the built-in MAINNET/TESTNET/STAGENET checkpoints, the per-block
checkpoint blob, and MoneroPulse checkpoint DNS -- are preserved here exactly as
found so the correction that follows is reviewable as a diff.

